{
  "requirement": "A named label carries decoded name parts. An anonymous label carries the hexadecimal identity hash.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum Label {\n    Named(Vec<String>),\n    Hash(String),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Label;\nimpl Debug for Label;\nimpl PartialEq for Label;\nimpl Eq for Label;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.outlines.Label`.\n\n**Obligations.**\n- (a) A named label carries decoded name parts, as `Named(Vec<String>)`.\n- (b) An anonymous label carries the hexadecimal identity hash, as `Hash(String)`.\n- (c) The enum has exactly this shape.\n- (d) It implements Clone, Debug, PartialEq and Eq.\n\n**Mapping to tests.**\n- (a) is covered by `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/selector.rs#mod[tests]/fn[parses_named_anonymous_and_ordinal_segments]`.\n  - It parses `impl[Thing/Trait%3CT%3E]/...` and asserts `segments[0].label == Label::Named([\"Thing\",\"Trait<T>\"])`. The percent-encoding is decoded and split into parts.\n  - It builds `Label::Named([\"a/b\",\"c d\"])` and checks the encoded base `impl[a%2Fb/c%20d]`.\n- (b) is covered by the same test. It parses `use@0123456789AB` and asserts `segments[2].label == Label::Hash(\"0123456789ab\")`. It also asserts the display form `use@0123456789ab`.\n- (d) is covered in two ways.\n  - Behaviourally: `assert_eq!` on Labels and Segments needs PartialEq and Debug. `segments[2].clone()` needs Clone on the Segment that contains a Label.\n  - Structurally: `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` runs `check_declaration`, which compares the trait-implementation list rustdoc publishes with the `impl ...` listing in the requirement. That catches a missing or extra Clone, Debug, PartialEq or Eq.\n- (c) is covered by the same `check_declaration`, which compares the published `Label` declaration (variants and payload types) with the requirement's Rust listing.\n\nBoth tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement or its public-API parent. No obligation is untested, and no marking gap exists.",
